NAME
    useradd - create a shell account

SYNOPSIS
    useradd <name>

DESCRIPTION
    Adds <name> to the process-wide account directory shared across all
    tmux(1) sessions. Only the 'root' account may add users. Accounts
    are stored in memory for the lifetime of the shell process.

EXAMPLES
    useradd guest

EXIT STATUS
    0   Account added.
    1   Missing name, caller is not root, or account already exists.

SEE ALSO
    userdel(1), su(1), passwd(1), who(1), whoami(1)
